1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:30,000
= kissasia.net =

2
00:00:27,433 --> 00:00:29,766
Rats... rats.

3
00:00:32,866 --> 00:00:34,066
So many rats.

4
00:00:37,033 --> 00:00:38,233
So many rats.

5
00:00:40,300 --> 00:00:42,933
So many... rats.

6
00:00:43,166 --> 00:00:46,333
S-so many

7
00:00:47,400 --> 00:00:48,400
rats...

8
00:01:00,700 --> 00:01:01,700
Xu Feiyu.

9
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:03,500
Don't be scared.

10
00:01:04,633 --> 00:01:05,666
I'm right here.

11
00:01:20,033 --> 00:01:21,933
Dad.

12
00:01:27,833 --> 00:01:29,666
Dad.

13
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:33,533
You came back.

14
00:01:43,933 --> 00:01:44,966
I always knew

15
00:01:45,033 --> 00:01:46,600
you'd come back...

16
00:01:49,500 --> 00:01:49,733
Yeah.

17
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:51,400
I'm back.

18
00:01:51,966 --> 00:01:52,966
Sleep.

19
00:02:01,266 --> 00:02:02,766
He's got a lousy temper

20
00:02:03,800 --> 00:02:05,600
but he's clearly still a kid.

21
00:02:07,266 --> 00:02:08,533
Old man...

22
00:02:09,300 --> 00:02:11,566
how could you bring yourself to leave him?

23
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:45,733
Song Yi?

24
00:02:47,200 --> 00:02:48,300
Song Yi.

25
00:02:51,033 --> 00:02:52,166
Song Yi?

26
00:02:55,666 --> 00:02:56,766
Song Yi?

27
00:03:15,100 --> 00:03:16,300
You're awake.

28
00:03:17,333 --> 00:03:18,433
Let me untie you.

29
00:03:19,200 --> 00:03:21,500
The knot I tied gets tighter
the more you pull.

30
00:03:23,900 --> 00:03:24,900
Song Yi.

31
00:03:25,100 --> 00:03:25,333
Hm?

32
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:26,833
I thought you left?

33
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:30,526
I was going to
but you still owe me my pay.

34
00:03:31,033 --> 00:03:32,532
Trying to get me for free?

35
00:03:32,533 --> 00:03:33,666
Then you may leave now.

36
00:03:34,100 --> 00:03:36,466
Yong Qi will pay you every cent.

37
00:03:36,733 --> 00:03:39,066
I looked after you at your bedside
all night.

38
00:03:39,800 --> 00:03:41,333
Doesn't that count for anything?

39
00:03:41,533 --> 00:03:43,032
Didn't I say you would be paid?

40
00:03:43,033 --> 00:03:44,533
You expect that from an employer?

41
00:03:47,100 --> 00:03:48,100
Tsk.

42
00:03:48,600 --> 00:03:51,132
Forget gratitude then,
you still have to eat

43
00:03:51,156 --> 00:03:52,156
I am not hungry.

44
00:03:52,266 --> 00:03:53,266
Whatever you order in

45
00:03:53,267 --> 00:03:54,766
will be added to your wages

46
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:56,466
I will pay for it.

47
00:03:58,700 --> 00:04:00,000
This time it's not delivery.

48
00:04:00,400 --> 00:04:01,800
I made this fish congee myself.

49
00:04:03,433 --> 00:04:03,666
Here.

50
00:04:04,033 --> 00:04:05,033
Come here.

51
00:04:06,866 --> 00:04:07,866
Sit.

52
00:04:12,433 --> 00:04:13,433
Take this.

53
00:04:14,600 --> 00:04:16,600
First time I've ever cooked for real.

54
00:04:17,166 --> 00:04:17,833
No nitpicking

55
00:04:17,833 --> 00:04:18,833
no picking it apart.

56
00:04:18,899 --> 00:04:19,332
Got issues?

57
00:04:19,766 --> 00:04:20,766
Hold it in.

58
00:04:43,433 --> 00:04:44,900
You're actually eating it.

59
00:04:46,500 --> 00:04:47,300
So tell me

60
00:04:47,466 --> 00:04:48,966
how does it taste…?

61
00:04:50,500 --> 00:04:51,533
Too much salt

62
00:04:52,100 --> 00:04:53,333
a bit too fishy

63
00:04:53,933 --> 00:04:55,166
not enough pepper

64
00:04:55,566 --> 00:04:56,566
and the heat was off.

65
00:04:57,100 --> 00:04:58,933
We agreed, no picking it apart.

66
00:05:00,100 --> 00:05:01,066
Still

67
00:05:01,067 --> 00:05:02,333
at least it's cooked.

68
00:05:04,366 --> 00:05:05,133
So I guess

69
00:05:05,166 --> 00:05:06,366
I did pretty well?

70
00:05:06,900 --> 00:05:08,366
I'll make it again tomorrow.

71
00:05:09,400 --> 00:05:11,666
You should know your own limits.

72
00:05:11,966 --> 00:05:12,966
No,

73
00:05:13,200 --> 00:05:14,200
let's order takeout.

74
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:16,066
You said it yourself,

75
00:05:16,233 --> 00:05:17,333
it's not me slacking off.

76
00:05:51,173 --> 00:05:52,639
There's one thing I don't get

77
00:05:53,166 --> 00:05:55,466
what's the fun in
doing a jigsaw blind?

78
00:06:02,200 --> 00:06:03,200
Never mind

79
00:06:03,300 --> 00:06:04,300
carry on.

80
00:06:07,600 --> 00:06:09,900
What do you think makes a puzzle fun?

81
00:06:10,300 --> 00:06:11,966
Putting the picture back together.

82
00:06:13,200 --> 00:06:15,833
Back to the sample image on the box.

83
00:06:16,133 --> 00:06:18,666
Only boring beginners do that.

84
00:06:23,733 --> 00:06:24,733
Hm.

85
00:06:25,266 --> 00:06:26,533
Nice job on this puzzle.

86
00:06:27,166 --> 00:06:28,433
Not one piece is right.

87
00:06:29,866 --> 00:06:30,932
Is there a problem?

88
00:06:30,933 --> 00:06:31,966
No problem.

89
00:06:33,200 --> 00:06:35,266
It's just that the way you think

90
00:06:36,466 --> 00:06:37,800
is a little out there.

91
00:06:45,933 --> 00:06:48,500
Feiyu, I'm going back in a few days.

92
00:06:48,633 --> 00:06:50,633
Yong Qi says you're changing carers again.

93
00:06:51,166 --> 00:06:52,732
I'll have her find you another

94
00:06:52,733 --> 00:06:54,200
but this is the last time.

95
00:06:54,900 --> 00:06:55,600
No need.

96
00:06:55,866 --> 00:06:57,133
Yong Qi's carer is still here.

97
00:06:57,326 --> 00:06:59,126
Didn't you drive him out?

98
00:06:59,333 --> 00:07:00,000
Feiyu.

99
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:03,156
The doctor said your sight
will come back before long.

100
00:07:03,210 --> 00:07:04,669
I'll get back as soon as I can,

101
00:07:04,700 --> 00:07:05,832
hold on a little longer.

102
00:07:05,833 --> 00:07:06,833
Got it.

103
00:07:10,800 --> 00:07:12,133
Guess I'll grit my teeth

104
00:07:12,300 --> 00:07:13,300
and hang on too.

105
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:15,233
No need to keep me around.

106
00:07:15,700 --> 00:07:17,066
Once your eyes are better

107
00:07:17,433 --> 00:07:18,733
we go our separate ways.

108
00:07:18,833 --> 00:07:19,833
Get it straight

109
00:07:20,333 --> 00:07:22,133
you're the one who won't leave.

110
00:07:23,566 --> 00:07:24,100
Fine

111
00:07:24,233 --> 00:07:25,233
I'll stay put.

112
00:07:26,066 --> 00:07:27,566
You cover food and board anyway.

113
00:07:27,800 --> 00:07:28,800
Oh right.

114
00:07:29,166 --> 00:07:30,233
Any plans later?

115
00:07:30,866 --> 00:07:31,733
If not

116
00:07:31,833 --> 00:07:32,833
I need to head out.

117
00:07:34,933 --> 00:07:36,833
Day one and you're asking for time off?

118
00:07:37,293 --> 00:07:39,126
You're the one who hates delivery!

119
00:07:39,300 --> 00:07:40,499
The fridge is empty

120
00:07:40,500 --> 00:07:41,966
so let me go do a grocery run.

121
00:07:44,733 --> 00:07:46,200
I could use a walk anyway...

122
00:07:46,866 --> 00:07:47,866
let's go together.

123
00:07:49,266 --> 00:07:50,266
Huh?

124
00:08:00,566 --> 00:08:02,700
Hello… hello…

125
00:08:05,200 --> 00:08:06,200
Hello…

126
00:08:07,333 --> 00:08:09,066
Who are you saying hi to?

127
00:08:11,666 --> 00:08:13,799
A lot of people are staring at us.

128
00:08:13,800 --> 00:08:14,999
This way

129
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:16,466
it won't be so awkward.

130
00:08:16,966 --> 00:08:17,600
Otherwise

131
00:08:17,766 --> 00:08:19,800
they'll think I'm out walking a dog.

132
00:08:19,866 --> 00:08:20,166
Ah.

133
00:08:20,733 --> 00:08:22,600
Don't read into it, I didn't mean you.

134
00:08:23,733 --> 00:08:25,000
I don't mind.

135
00:08:25,766 --> 00:08:27,233
The way they see it

136
00:08:27,533 --> 00:08:29,733
I'm the one walking a guide dog.

137
00:08:33,033 --> 00:08:35,700
Forget this crappy stick

138
00:08:36,033 --> 00:08:37,033
I'll help you walk.

139
00:08:37,366 --> 00:08:38,366
Here.

140
00:08:59,633 --> 00:09:00,700
I can walk on my own.

141
00:09:01,933 --> 00:09:03,199
This is a supermarket.

142
00:09:03,200 --> 00:09:04,599
If you break something

143
00:09:04,600 --> 00:09:05,733
you're paying for it.

144
00:09:09,666 --> 00:09:10,033
Hey

145
00:09:10,066 --> 00:09:11,300
watch your step.

146
00:09:27,033 --> 00:09:27,200
Huh?

147
00:09:27,566 --> 00:09:28,566
Nice, bread crisps.

148
00:09:31,433 --> 00:09:32,433
This works too.

149
00:09:36,500 --> 00:09:37,766
Wafer rolls look good.

150
00:09:44,466 --> 00:09:45,466
Choco pies.

151
00:09:52,433 --> 00:09:52,733
Ooh!

152
00:09:52,933 --> 00:09:54,266
Chips!

153
00:09:54,933 --> 00:09:55,933
Chips are good too.

154
00:10:02,333 --> 00:10:02,700
Hey, why

155
00:10:02,766 --> 00:10:03,766
did you put it all back?

156
00:10:03,767 --> 00:10:06,033
No junk food in the house.

157
00:10:06,300 --> 00:10:07,365
Even if it's junk

158
00:10:07,366 --> 00:10:08,833
it's junk that makes you happy.

159
00:10:09,600 --> 00:10:10,600
Xu Feiyu.

160
00:10:10,700 --> 00:10:12,800
Did you have no snacks as a kid?

161
00:10:13,700 --> 00:10:14,700
That's just sad.

162
00:10:15,100 --> 00:10:16,100
So

163
00:10:16,200 --> 00:10:17,800
can we at least get instant noodles?

164
00:10:18,166 --> 00:10:19,533
No.

165
00:10:19,566 --> 00:10:20,800
If you won't buy anything

166
00:10:20,966 --> 00:10:22,333
why come to the supermarket?

167
00:10:22,700 --> 00:10:23,066
Fine.

168
00:10:23,366 --> 00:10:24,366
You tell me then.

169
00:10:24,600 --> 00:10:25,833
What can we actually buy?

170
00:10:25,966 --> 00:10:27,633
You're the one who wanted to come

171
00:10:27,900 --> 00:10:28,966
and now you ask me?

172
00:10:29,033 --> 00:10:30,233
It's your money

173
00:10:30,333 --> 00:10:31,366
so I'm asking you.

174
00:10:31,966 --> 00:10:33,366
I am the one who pays you.

175
00:10:33,700 --> 00:10:35,033
What to buy is your job.

176
00:10:35,133 --> 00:10:35,600
Stop.

177
00:10:36,133 --> 00:10:37,166
I surrender!

178
00:10:46,166 --> 00:10:47,600
Just stay right here

179
00:10:47,700 --> 00:10:49,000
and don't wander off.

180
00:10:50,800 --> 00:10:51,466
I'm going in

181
00:10:51,467 --> 00:10:52,832
to shop by myself.

182
00:10:52,833 --> 00:10:54,033
I promise, no junk food.

183
00:10:54,433 --> 00:10:54,900
That way

184
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:55,566
we're good?

185
00:10:55,800 --> 00:10:57,532
Sunflower seeds, buy one get one free.

186
00:10:57,533 --> 00:11:00,166
The flavorings and colorings
are over the limit.

187
00:11:00,633 --> 00:11:02,132
This is junk food too.

188
00:11:02,133 --> 00:11:03,133
You…

189
00:12:24,700 --> 00:12:27,865
Manufacturer's special, sunflower seeds
buy one get one free

190
00:12:27,866 --> 00:12:29,533
bread, buy two get one free.

191
00:12:30,133 --> 00:12:31,400
Today only.

192
00:12:31,966 --> 00:12:32,966
Feiyu.

193
00:12:33,300 --> 00:12:34,300
Xu Feiyu!

194
00:12:45,866 --> 00:12:46,933
Xu Feiyu.

195
00:12:53,733 --> 00:12:54,733
Excuse me.

196
00:12:54,733 --> 00:12:55,733
Can I borrow this?

197
00:12:55,966 --> 00:12:56,800
Oh, sure.

198
00:12:56,800 --> 00:12:57,800
Thanks.

199
00:12:58,866 --> 00:12:59,966
Xu Feiyu!

200
00:13:01,100 --> 00:13:02,700
Xu Feiyu, where'd you go?

201
00:13:08,566 --> 00:13:09,233
Xu Feiyu!

202
00:13:09,234 --> 00:13:10,465
Hey, you're taking it?

203
00:13:10,466 --> 00:13:11,266
Xu Feiyu!

204
00:13:11,400 --> 00:13:11,600
Hey.

205
00:13:11,766 --> 00:13:12,832
Watch this for me.

206
00:13:12,833 --> 00:13:14,065
Xu Feiyu, you idiot.

207
00:13:14,066 --> 00:13:15,365
Hey! What's wrong with you!

208
00:13:15,366 --> 00:13:17,065
Told you not to run off!

209
00:13:17,066 --> 00:13:18,066
Xu Feiyu!

210
00:13:21,433 --> 00:13:22,766
Xu Feiyu!

211
00:13:23,833 --> 00:13:25,100
Where'd you go? Xu Feiyu.

212
00:13:28,133 --> 00:13:29,466
Xu Feiyu!

213
00:13:35,133 --> 00:13:36,133
Xu Feiyu!

214
00:13:36,800 --> 00:13:37,832
I told you to stay put.

215
00:13:37,833 --> 00:13:39,100
Why'd you come out here.

216
00:13:40,466 --> 00:13:41,733
I just found this.

217
00:13:44,033 --> 00:13:45,066
What are you, three?

218
00:13:45,533 --> 00:13:46,533
Do you have any idea

219
00:13:46,534 --> 00:13:47,799
how dangerous this is?

220
00:13:47,800 --> 00:13:49,932
You're the one who left me there alone.

221
00:13:49,933 --> 00:13:50,366
I…

222
00:13:50,633 --> 00:13:52,266
Now you're worried about danger?

223
00:13:53,266 --> 00:13:54,033
I'm sorry.

224
00:13:54,033 --> 00:13:54,766
There, said it.

225
00:13:54,933 --> 00:13:55,933
What was that?

226
00:13:56,433 --> 00:13:57,133
Didn't hear you...

227
00:13:57,133 --> 00:13:58,133
I said!

228
00:13:58,200 --> 00:13:58,600
I!

229
00:13:58,733 --> 00:13:59,066
AM!

230
00:13:59,200 --> 00:13:59,800
SORRY!

231
00:13:59,833 --> 00:14:01,832
Jeez, jeez.

232
00:14:01,833 --> 00:14:02,865
Hey, mister.

233
00:14:02,866 --> 00:14:03,633
You all right?

234
00:14:03,634 --> 00:14:04,700
What is wrong with you.

235
00:14:05,433 --> 00:14:06,666
I lent it to call someone

236
00:14:06,766 --> 00:14:08,433
and you run off with it?

237
00:14:08,933 --> 00:14:10,465
I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

238
00:14:10,466 --> 00:14:11,466
You're insane!

239
00:14:11,733 --> 00:14:13,000
Better not be broken.

240
00:14:13,933 --> 00:14:15,233
I was in a panic just now.

241
00:14:15,600 --> 00:14:17,300
Xu Feiyu, you idiot.

242
00:14:17,633 --> 00:14:18,533
Told you not to run off!

243
00:14:18,633 --> 00:14:19,333
Okay, it's fine.

244
00:14:19,333 --> 00:14:20,333
Xu Feiyu!

245
00:14:20,366 --> 00:14:21,266
Song Yi!

246
00:14:21,266 --> 00:14:22,266
This guy, I swear.

247
00:14:22,766 --> 00:14:24,033
What are you saying!

248
00:14:26,533 --> 00:14:27,533
Good, you're okay.

249
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:30,133
Don't touch me!

250
00:14:31,233 --> 00:14:31,533
Come on

251
00:14:31,633 --> 00:14:32,300
let's go home.

252
00:14:32,301 --> 00:14:33,999
Don't touch me.

253
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:34,466
Come on

254
00:14:34,467 --> 00:14:35,533
I can walk on my own.

255
00:14:36,266 --> 00:14:37,266
Come on now.

256
00:14:58,033 --> 00:14:59,033
That's it?

257
00:14:59,600 --> 00:15:00,666
He hides his key exactly

258
00:15:01,033 --> 00:15:02,033
like my old man.

259
00:16:13,733 --> 00:16:14,733
Whoa!

260
00:16:15,500 --> 00:16:16,733
You scared me.

261
00:16:16,833 --> 00:16:17,833
What are you doing?

262
00:16:18,833 --> 00:16:20,133
Song Yi...

263
00:16:20,666 --> 00:16:22,533
who said you could come in here?

264
00:16:22,966 --> 00:16:23,966
What's wrong?

265
00:16:24,033 --> 00:16:25,400
I came to clean up.

266
00:16:25,666 --> 00:16:27,200
This place is filthy.

267
00:16:28,166 --> 00:16:29,166
Oh right, Xu Feiyu.

268
00:16:29,766 --> 00:16:30,600
In this photo

269
00:16:30,766 --> 00:16:32,033
is that the three of you?

270
00:16:32,400 --> 00:16:34,300
Get out!

271
00:16:36,133 --> 00:16:37,600
I was just asking

272
00:16:37,733 --> 00:16:38,733
and you're mad again.

273
00:16:39,266 --> 00:16:40,933
I said get out!

274
00:16:41,266 --> 00:16:41,766
Fine!

275
00:16:41,933 --> 00:16:43,000
If you hate it, I won't…

276
00:16:43,100 --> 00:16:44,000
Get out! Get out!

277
00:16:44,100 --> 00:16:46,000
Now! Get! Out!

278
00:16:47,033 --> 00:16:47,533
Ugh

279
00:16:47,800 --> 00:16:48,800
this guy, honestly.

280
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:44,666
And I thought he was back to normal.

281
00:17:47,266 --> 00:17:49,400
He could've come at you with a knife.

282
00:17:49,600 --> 00:17:50,766
For years now

283
00:17:50,933 --> 00:17:53,000
even his own mother won't go in that room.

284
00:17:53,366 --> 00:17:54,566
You're really something.

285
00:17:54,633 --> 00:17:55,866
How was I supposed to know?

286
00:17:56,300 --> 00:17:57,300
Besides

287
00:17:57,700 --> 00:17:59,100
if it stays shut, it doesn't exist?

288
00:17:59,933 --> 00:18:01,600
That's just lying to yourself.

289
00:18:02,566 --> 00:18:05,032
Could you use your head for once.

290
00:18:05,033 --> 00:18:06,933
Not everything is a joke.

291
00:18:07,600 --> 00:18:08,600
Yong Qi

292
00:18:09,200 --> 00:18:11,066
from a psychology standpoint

293
00:18:11,400 --> 00:18:13,400
how do you fix Xu Feiyu's problem?

294
00:18:20,300 --> 00:18:22,600
Ever since Mr. Song passed

295
00:18:23,066 --> 00:18:25,166
he's been sure there are rats in his room.

296
00:18:28,500 --> 00:18:29,566
The rats in here.

297
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:31,000
Can you catch them?

298
00:18:32,433 --> 00:18:33,566
So that's a hallucination.

299
00:18:34,333 --> 00:18:35,133
I'll cure him.

300
00:18:35,133 --> 00:18:36,133
Song Yi.

301
00:18:36,333 --> 00:18:37,766
Stop messing around already.

302
00:18:38,066 --> 00:18:40,033
Either you go back to Singapore now

303
00:18:40,133 --> 00:18:41,500
or look after him a few days.

304
00:18:41,766 --> 00:18:42,833
Don't stir up trouble.

305
00:18:43,833 --> 00:18:45,966
I was only trying to help.

306
00:18:49,900 --> 00:18:51,100
Good intentions

307
00:18:51,300 --> 00:18:53,300
don't always end well.

308
00:18:54,266 --> 00:18:55,300
Think about it.

309
00:18:55,833 --> 00:18:58,166
If Song Yang hadn't shown up back then

310
00:18:58,633 --> 00:19:00,600
how would your world have turned out?

311
00:19:01,500 --> 00:19:04,333
That's tomato and egg stir-fry done…

312
00:19:06,933 --> 00:19:07,933
Hey, Song Yi!

313
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:09,000
Huh?

314
00:19:10,766 --> 00:19:12,266
Did you learn this dish or not?

315
00:19:13,333 --> 00:19:13,833
Uh…

316
00:19:13,900 --> 00:19:14,900
Where were we?

317
00:19:15,166 --> 00:19:17,200
Take my advice and just give up

318
00:19:17,366 --> 00:19:18,600
because for you

319
00:19:18,666 --> 00:19:19,400
studying

320
00:19:19,600 --> 00:19:20,966
is way easier than cooking.

321
00:19:21,966 --> 00:19:22,966
Oh crap.

322
00:19:23,166 --> 00:19:24,500
Yong Qi, I'm dead, I gotta go.

323
00:19:24,666 --> 00:19:26,100
I cut class and forgot to call in.
